  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Which of the following data sets **might** be normally distributed?",
  "worked_solution": "If a large data set is normally distributed, it should be approximately bell-shaped. \n\nAmong the given options, the only bell-shaped curve is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14178098/assets/342a545437fc0884e69bb31d383a6e121c9cb0a1db08eab4d702cf9a0b296075.png)\n\nIt's important to note that other bell-shaped distributions exist. Therefore, further tests on the data are required to confirm whether the underlying distribution is normal.",
